@hostname = http://localhost:5049


@ContentType = application/json


###
### Test Case 1: Anonymous Request (Should return 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{hostname}}/api/assessments/results

###

### Test Case 2: Authenticated Request (Should return 200 OK with JSON)
GET {{hostname}}/api/assessments/results
X-Training-User: user1
###
### Test Case 3: Worker Smoke Test
###
GET {{hostname}}/api/enrollments/worker-smoke
X-Training-User: user2
###


### 1. Create an Enrollment (POST)
# This will generate a new record and return a 201 Created with a Location header.
POST {{hostname}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: {{ContentType}}

{
  "studentId": "S-100",
  "courseCode": "CS-101"
}

### 2. Get All Enrollments (GET)
# Verify the record you just created exists in the system array.
GET {{hostname}}/api/enrollments
Accept: {{ContentType}}

### 3. Trigger ProblemDetails Standardized Error (GET)
# Exercise 6: This calls your broken route to verify the RFC 9457 JSON error payload shape.
GET {{hostname}}/api/error
Accept: application/problem+json

### 4. Fetch a Non-Existent Record (GET 404)
# Exercise 6: Verifies UseStatusCodePages() converts empty 404s into standard ProblemDetails shapes.
GET {{hostname}}/api/enrollments/does-not-exist
Accept: application/problem+json

### Test Scalar UI in Dev Mode
GET http://localhost:5049/scalar/v1

### Test average gpa
GET http://localhost:5049/api/reports/average-gpa
Accept: application/json
 

 
